Joern bytecode frontend (jimple2cpg) - code-property graph build record
harness/artifacts/logs/cpg-frontend.log
================================================================================

WHAT THIS FILE ESTABLISHES

  The invocation of the Joern bytecode frontend that wrote the code-property
  graph this run scans and queries: the preconditions that had to hold before it
  ran, its exact command line, the JDK major version and the heap it ran under,
  the identity of the graph it produced measured from the bytes on disk, and the
  two metrics the frontend itself reported - duplicate-class overwrites and
  AST-creation failures.

  The graph is read three more times after it is written: the importCpg
  verification load, the Stage 3 Joern runner, and each Stage 5 probe query. The
  byte size and sha256 recorded in PHASE 3 are the identity every one of those
  loads re-verifies, and a mismatch at any of them halts the run (AAP 0.6.4,
  0.8.2). Getting that pair wrong is not subtle but it is late: the Joern runner
  guards its input and exits 78 naming the missing graph, so a record describing
  the wrong bytes would sail past that guard and every downstream conclusion
  would be about a graph nobody has.

