STATUS - READ THIS BEFORE ANY NUMBER BELOW
================================================================================

  The frontend was NOT re-invoked by this run. The graph at the resolved path
  was written on 2026-08-24 at 13:52:22Z by the provisioning invocation
  reproduced in PHASE 2, and every byte-level figure in PHASE 3 was measured
  from that file, live, by the commands shown in this file.

  Why it was not re-invoked, stated as the two things that would have happened
  if it had been. The resolved path is host-global and shared: the environment's
  own instructions list /opt/blitzy-harness/cpg/spark.cpg as "SHARED, READ-ONLY,
  SAFE FOR CONCURRENT USE - never restart, re-seed, re-clone, delete", with up
  to 45 concurrent clones on this host and the warning that "a sibling is
  probably mid-scan against them", and they state plainly under DO NOT: "rebuild
  the graph". Writing through the symlink would therefore replace bytes a
  sibling clone is reading part-way through a 12-minute importCpg load or a
  734-second Joern scan. Writing a fresh graph anywhere else would leave
  $HARNESS_CPG - which is what harness/bin/run-joern.sh actually resolves and
  loads - pointing at these same provisioning bytes, so this file would then
  record an identity for a graph no later stage ever loads. That is exactly the
  failure this record exists to prevent.

  What that costs, stated rather than smoothed over. AAP 0.1.1 requires the
  graph to be created by this run and never accepts a graph already on disk as
  this run's output; that requirement is NOT satisfied, and it is carried below
  as divergence D1, a halt-class finding reported rather than repaired (AAP
  0.8.1). The input set the documented invocation was given is 62 archives from
  31 modules, not the 191 own artifacts from 38 projects that this run's
  full-reactor build produced and this run's inventory staged and proved; that
  is divergence D2. Neither is reconciled by adjusting a number, and nothing was
  excluded from any input set to make a count fit.

  What remains true and checkable. Every measurement in this file is either
  taken live here from the artefact itself, or recounted here from the
  frontend's own preserved output stream - which is carried in APPENDIX A in
  full, verbatim, so that any figure in PHASE 4 can be re-derived from it. No
  figure is copied from another document as a measurement: where another
  document states the same value, this file re-derives it and says so. The
  identity in PHASE 3 is the identity of exactly the bytes the Stage 3 Joern
  runner and the Stage 5 probe queries will load.

================================================================================
HOW TO READ THIS FILE
================================================================================

  Plain text, append-only, in execution order. Every step is a command line
  introduced by '$ ', followed by its captured streams and its exit status:

      [stdout]  ... verbatim; nothing follows the marker when the stream was empty
      [stderr]  ... verbatim; java, stat and ls failures write here, not to stdout
      [exit]    ... the command's exit status, then the UTC time it started and
                    the seconds it took

  Every table in PHASE 4 is the verbatim stdout of the command shown immediately
  above it, so no figure in this file is hand-transcribed from a table into
  prose. Commands that read a JSON document print the fields they read; commands
  that count print the count. Nothing is summarised, reflowed or elided, and no
  measurement is fabricated.

  Each command was run with 'harness/env.sh' sourced in a fresh non-login shell
  from the repository root, which is how every runner in this harness is
  invoked. Where a command had to run from somewhere else, its working directory
  is named: joern and jimple2cpg write an ~800 MB ./workspace into whatever
  directory they are started from, so they are started from this clone's private
  scratch directory and never from the repository.

================================================================================
METHOD - THE FOUR PRINCIPLES THIS FILE IS HELD TO
================================================================================

  review_rules returned exactly 'No user rules provided.' for the whole
  document. That is a complete read, corroborated by AAP 0.7 and 0.10.2. No
  user-specified rule governs this file, and the absence is not read as licence
  to lower the bar; enterprise best practice is substituted, held to the AAP's
  own four principles.

  P1 Verification is independent of the thing verified (AAP 0.1.3). The graph's
  identity is measured from the bytes on disk, not inferred from the frontend
  reporting success: PHASE 3 stats and hashes the file itself. The two frontend
  metrics are recounted here from the preserved stream by commands whose output
  is present, rather than quoted from the record that also states them - and the
  recount agreeing with the record is the point of doing it twice.

  P2 Reject rather than infer (AAP 0.1.3). The frontend's overwrite warning
  names the DESTINATION class file, never the archive whose definition survived,
  so NO WINNER MAP APPEARS ANYWHERE IN THIS FILE. What PHASE 4 reports instead
  is containment - which modules' and which artifacts' archives contain an entry
  of that name, measured by reading the archives - and containment is labelled
  as containment every time it is used.

  P3 Halt-and-report over silent repair (AAP 0.8.1). Nothing was excluded from
  any input set to make a count fit, no heap was lowered, and the two conditions
  this run could not satisfy are reported as divergences with both values rather
  than quietly reconciled. Lowering a heap is prohibited outright: it produces a
  truncated graph whose silence is indistinguishable from a clean result.

  P4 Verbatim preservation (AAP 0.1.3). The frontend's own output is retained as
  emitted, complete, in APPENDIX A, with its byte size and sha256 stated so the
  copy can be checked against the source.

================================================================================
VERDICT VOCABULARY
================================================================================

  PASS                : the condition was measured here and it holds.
  RECORDED DIFFERENCE : observed differs from expected; both values are recorded
                        and the run continues (AAP 0.9.3).
  HALT-CLASS FINDING  : a condition AAP 0.9.2 or 0.1.1 treats as halting. It is
                        reported with both values and NOT repaired; nothing is
                        installed, rebuilt, trimmed or overwritten to clear it.
  INCONCLUSIVE        : the measurement could not be made. Named, never guessed.

