STEP 10 - How jimple2cpg is invoked, and what pins its JDK
  The wrapper is what makes every Joern process land on JDK 21: it exports
  JAVA_HOME from JAVA_HOME_21 before exec'ing the joern-cli launcher, whose own
  script would otherwise inherit the host default of 17.

$ cat /opt/blitzy-tools/bin/jimple2cpg
[stdout]
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Blitzy provisioning wrapper: pins Joern 4.0.607 to Temurin JDK 21 (JAVA_HOME_21).
# Joern 4.x documents JDK 21 as its tested requirement; the host default java is 17 for the Spark build.
set -u
JAVA_HOME_21="${JAVA_HOME_21:-/opt/blitzy-tools/jdk/jdk-21.0.12.1+1}"
export JAVA_HOME="$JAVA_HOME_21"
export PATH="$JAVA_HOME/bin:$PATH"
